# TMS Core Standards

Ticket Management System — Java 21, Spring Boot 3.x, Gradle, PostgreSQL/H2, REST, React.

## Non-Negotiables

- Business logic in **service** classes only; controllers are HTTP adapters
- Constructor injection; no field injection
- Throw `TmsException(ErrorCode.*)` — never raw runtime exceptions for domain errors
- Methods ≤ 50 lines; decompose when longer
- Lombok on DTOs only
- Secrets never in source, logs, or committed config

## Authoritative File References

| Concern | Path |
|---------|------|
| Dependencies | `build.gradle` |
| Properties | `src/main/resources/application.yml` |
| Config properties | `com.tms.common.config.TmsConfig` |
| Security config | `com.tms.common.config.SecurityConfiguration`, `CommonConfiguration` |
| API helpers | `com.tms.common.util.AppUtil` |
| Security helpers | `com.tms.common.util.SecurityUtil` |
| Shared utilities | `com.tms.common.util.Util` — search before creating |
| Exceptions | `com.tms.common.exception.TmsException` |
| Error codes | `com.tms.common.enums.ErrorCode` |
| Prompt history | `docs/prompt-history.md` — append every AI prompt |

## Package Layout

`com.tms.<domain>.{controller,service,repository,model.{entity,dto}}`
Shared code under `com.tms.common.{config,enums,exception,util}`.
